  m_Name: AxialPistonPumpData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Axial Piston Pump
  engineDescription: "An Axial Piston Pump is a positive displacement hydraulic pump
    that converts mechanical energy into hydraulic energy by using multiple pistons
    arranged parallel to the drive shaft. Its main components are the cylinder block,
    pistons, swash plate, drive shaft, valve plate, and housing. During operation,
    the rotating cylinder block causes the pistons to reciprocate against the angled
    swash plate, drawing hydraulic fluid into the pump and delivering it under high
    pressure. \nAxial piston pumps are widely used in construction equipment, aircraft
    hydraulic systems, industrial machinery, agricultural equipment, and mobile hydraulic
    applications. From an engineering perspective, understanding pump displacement,
    pressure rating, volumetric efficiency, mechanical efficiency, lubrication, and
    maintenance is essential for proper pump selection, reliable operation, and energy-efficient
    hydraulic system performance."
  engineCategory: Engineering
